35:Study data is from the ABIDE I and ABIDE II collections of the ABIDE initiative (N = 2226). Only males and participants under age 14 years were included in the study, resulting in a study sample size of N = 816. The study dataset was then split into training and testing datasets. The training dataset was composed of 80% of healthy controls (N = 321), while the testing dataset was composed of the remaining 20% of healthy controls (N = 77) and ASD patients (N = 418). Further analysis with behavioral outcomes were performed only in ASD patients and analysis sample size was based on data availability.
41:<!-- image -->
43:Fig S2: Histograms showing age distribution of training (N = 321) and testing (N = 495) datasets.
47:<!-- image -->
49:Fig S3: The ABIDE dataset was harmonized across 18 batches (Supplementary Table 1) based on site and scan parameters using the neuroCombat package. Boxplots display the spread of functional connectivity across the batches before and after harmonization. The VNxDAN connectivity is shown as an example as the between-network connectivity with the highest batch effects (Supplementary Tables 3a-b).
